81
00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:59.250
In this case, the blueprints is not a form of movement component,

82
00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.250
and therefore the target must have a connection.

83
00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.379
So don't worry too much about that.

84
00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:13.379
That means that this is an incorrect function for the actor class.

85
00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:18.500
But it's just there as an example to show you what

86
00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.500
the code compile looks like if it fails.

87
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.110
Next up, we have Difference.

88
00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.110
Now this is part of source control.

89
00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.110
Don't need to worry about it for this course,

90
00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:33.110
but it will allow you to see what's been changed from one version to the next.

91
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:39.430
Fine, this will give you an option to search for a specific example.

92
00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.430
Begin Play, help me move to the Begin Play node.

93
00:06:45.009 --> 00:06:46.009
Hide unrelated.

